A||||1||mshill||A/C High Pressure Switch Shorted...||||11||
Z||000000||mshill||03-13-2000||02:05 AM||||Prior to removing my engine (disconnected the A/C unit as well) the A/C worked fine and the radiator fan came on when it was supposed to.  Now, after getting the cradle back in after the rebuild (and thorough cleaning of accessories) it seems the fan would run all the time.  I tracked it down to the A/C high pressure switch being stuck closed.  <P>Can this be seperated from the A/C compressor?  Could this be closed if the system had been evacuated?<P>What should I do?||||reg||11
Z||000001||theogre||03-13-2000||06:53 PM||||high is closed? I believe it's suposed to be. Should open only if pressure gets too high as I recall. It's the last thing before system venting.<P>check your fan relay, and your temp switch wire. You could have fan running if you wrecked the wire to the switch. The AC control of the fan is done in the controls up on the dash as far as I know.||||reg||1
